<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id=queue-affinity>Queue Affinity<a href=#queue-affinity class=hash-link aria-label="Direct link to Queue Affinity" title="Direct link to Queue Affinity" translate=no>​</a></h3>
<p>Applications can declare queue affinity rules when opening a connection.
The client library will do its best to connect to an appropriate node to enforce these rules.
This can result in lower intra-cluster traffic, reducing latency and increasing throughput.</p>
<p>In the following example we declare "publish" affinity on a given connection.
The library will connect to a node that hosts the queue leader.
It will also reuse a connection with the same affinity if the environment has already created one.</p>
